---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const buildDate = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Who runs Kerala Web Watch, why it exists, and how to contact or contribute."
  altLangHref="/ml/about/"
  altLangLabel="മലയാളം"
>
  <h1>About Kerala Web Watch</h1>

  <p>
    Kerala Web Watch is an independent, open-source civic project. It is <strong>not</strong> an
    official Government of Kerala service and is not affiliated with any department it audits.
    It exists so a citizen can check, in plain language, whether a government website works right
    now, and so a webmaster can see exactly what to fix.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Source and issue tracker:
    <a href="https://github.com/hashin/kerala-web-watch">github.com/hashin/kerala-web-watch</a>.
    A public contact email is not yet set (tracked as an open question in the project's own
    <a href="https://github.com/hashin/kerala-web-watch/blob/main/docs/STATE.md">STATE.md</a>) &mdash;
    until then, please use a GitHub issue.
  </p>

  <h2>Contribute</h2>
  <p>
    Found a site we're missing, or a wrong entry? Open an issue or a pull request against the
    <a href="https://github.com/hashin/kerala-web-watch/tree/main/registry">registry</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <p>
    We aim for WCAG 2.1 AA on our own pages: semantic HTML, a skip link, visible keyboard focus,
    and status that is never conveyed by colour alone. This site is itself entered in the registry
    (id <code>kerala-web-watch</code>) and audited like any other, so its own accessibility score
    is a real, checkable number on <a href="/sites/kerala-web-watch/">its own site page</a>, not a
    claim taken on trust. Found a barrier? Please <a href="#contact">tell us</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="screen-reader">Screen reader access</h2>
  <p>
    This site is built from plain semantic HTML (headings, lists, tables, landmarks) with no
    custom widgets that override standard screen-reader behaviour, other than the search box
    (a third-party "Pagefind" search widget, self-hosted, keyboard operable). A skip link at the
    top of every page jumps straight to the main content.
  </p>

  <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    No cookies, no analytics, no third-party requests of any kind on this site. Fonts are
    self-hosted. See <a href="/fonts/OFL.txt">/fonts/OFL.txt</a> for the Malayalam typeface's
    licence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="terms">Terms and conditions</h2>
  <p>
    Use this site and its published data as you like, within the licences below. There is no
    account to create and nothing to agree to before reading it. This project accepts no liability
    for decisions made based on its findings &mdash; see the Disclaimer below.
  </p>

  <h2 id="copyright-policy">Copyright policy</h2>
  <p>
    Code is MIT-licensed; the registry and audit data are CC-BY-4.0. Both are in the
    <a href="https://github.com/hashin/kerala-web-watch">repository</a>, including each licence's
    full text. Screenshots of audited government websites are included only as audit evidence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hyperlinking-policy">Hyperlinking policy</h2>
  <p>
    Every government website this project links to is public information already; you're welcome
    to link to any page on this site without asking first. We are not responsible for the content
    of external sites we link to, government or otherwise, and a link from us is not an endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimer">Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    This is an independent, unofficial project, not a Government of Kerala service. It has no
    legal or administrative authority over any department. Every finding is a starting point for a
    department to verify and fix, not a final verdict &mdash; see the
    <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> for exactly how each check works and its
    limitations.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rti">Right to Information (RTI)</h2>
  <p>
    This project is not a government body or a "public authority" under the Right to Information
    Act, so RTI requests do not apply to it. For RTI requests about a specific department, use
    that department's own RTI/PIO contact &mdash; audited government sites are checked
    (<code>gigw.rti</code>) for whether they publish one.
  </p>

  <h2 id="licence">Licence</h2>
  <p>
    Code is MIT-licensed; the registry and audit data are CC-BY-4.0. Both are in the
    <a href="https://github.com/hashin/kerala-web-watch">repository</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/sitemap-index.xml">Sitemap</a> &middot; Last updated {buildDate}
  </p>
</Layout>
